<%#
kind: PXEGrub2
name: AlmaLinux 10 bootc PXEGrub2
model: ProvisioningTemplate
oses:
- AlmaLinux 10
description: |
  UEFI (PXEGrub2) boot entry for AlmaLinux 10 image-mode (bootc) provisioning.

  The bootc payload is installed by `ostreecontainer` in the kickstart, but
  Anaconda's installer RUNTIME (stage2 = images/install.img) still has to be
  fetched over the network. That is what `inst.stage2` provides here.

  stage2 is auto-derived from the host's assigned installation medium (the
  synced AlmaLinux 10 BaseOS kickstart repo). If you'd rather pin it, set host
  parameter `kickstart_kernel_custom_options` to include inst.stage2=... and
  this template will use that and skip the derived value.

  NOTE: this is the UEFI (linuxefi/initrdefi) variant — correct for modern
  AlmaLinux 10 VMs. For legacy BIOS hosts, use a PXELinux template instead.
%>
<%
  # Install tree containing the Anaconda stage2 image (images/install.img).
  install_tree = @host.operatingsystem.medium_uri(@host)

  # Extra kernel args from host param; accept an array or a plain string.
  # Duck-type instead of is_a?(Array): safemode forbids the Array constant.
  custom = host_param('kickstart_kernel_custom_options')
  custom = custom.join(' ') if custom.respond_to?(:join)
  custom = custom.to_s

  # Only derive inst.stage2 if the param didn't already supply it.
  stage2 = custom.include?('inst.stage2') ? '' : "inst.stage2=#{install_tree}"
%>
set default=0
set timeout=10

menuentry 'Provision <%= @host.name %> (AlmaLinux 10 image-mode)' --id provision {
  linuxefi <%= @kernel %> ks=<%= foreman_url('provision') %> inst.ks.sendmac <%= stage2 %> <%= pxe_kernel_options %> <%= custom %>
  initrdefi <%= @initrd %>
}
